# RenderType.create is package-private and RenderType has no public constructor, so there is no
# vanilla or Fabric API path to a custom render layer. TrarnCore needs one: drawing highlights
# through terrain requires a pipeline whose depth test always passes, and no vanilla layer combines
# that with a lines or quads vertex format.
#
# Declaring it here opens it once for the whole family — consuming mods call Layers.seeThroughLines()
# and never touch RenderType.create themselves.
#
# Minecraft 26.x ships unobfuscated, so this is written in Mojang's own names; there is no
# intermediary to remap through. In 1.21.11 this same entry named RenderLayer.of instead.
#
# Note that RenderLayer still exists in 26.x as net/minecraft/client/renderer/entity/layers/RenderLayer,
# which is an entity feature layer and an entirely unrelated thing. RenderType is what we want.
accessible	method	net/minecraft/client/renderer/rendertype/RenderType	create	(Ljava/lang/String;Lnet/minecraft/client/renderer/rendertype/RenderSetup;)Lnet/minecraft/client/renderer/rendertype/RenderType;
